      {
        "question_text": "Estimate:\n(a) $8\\times57$ by rounding $57$ to the nearest $10$\n(b) $6\\times453$ by rounding $453$ to the nearest $100$\n(c) $7\\times250$ by rounding $250$ to the nearest $100$.",
        "solution_text": "Keep the one-digit factor unchanged.\n(a) $57$ rounds to $60$.\n$8\\times57\\approx8\\times60=480$\n(b) $453$ is nearer to $500$ than $400$.\n$6\\times453\\approx6\\times500=3000$\n(c) $250$ is halfway between $200$ and $300$. Round up to $300$.\n$7\\times250\\approx7\\times300=2100$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Estimate $4\\times638$ by rounding $638$ to the nearest $100$.",
        "solution_text": "$638$ is nearer to $600$ than $700$.\n$4\\times638\\approx4\\times600=2400$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Estimate $3\\times286$ by rounding $286$ to the nearest $100$.",
        "solution_text": "$286$ is nearer to $300$ than $200$.\n$3\\times286\\approx3\\times300=900$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Estimate $9\\times724$ by rounding each factor to $1$ significant figure.",
        "solution_text": "The one-digit factor $9$ stays unchanged. The first non-zero digit in $724$ is in the hundreds place, so round to the nearest hundred: $724\\approx700$.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}9\\times724\\\\&\\approx9\\times700\\\\&=6300\\end{aligned}$"
      }
    ],
